$DATUM (S)-Methyl
3-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)-4-(4-(3-((4-methoxypyridin-2-yl)amino)propoxy)phenyl)butanoate
(8). Compound 10 (550 mg of crude product) was dissolved in absolute DCM.
Next, 2-amino-4-methoxypyridine (0.21 mg, 1.73 mmol) and magnesium
sulfate monohydrate (0.87 mg, 6.27 mmol) were added. After the suspension
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature, sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(1.71 g, 8.07 mmol) was added, and stirring was continued overnight.
After addition of 50 mL of a saturated NaHCO3 solution and further 30 min
of stirring, the organic layer was extracted twice with DCM (50 mL) and
dried over Na2SO4. After filtration, the solution was concentrated to
dryness and the crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(DCM/EtOAc 1:1) to give 8. Colorless oil, yield (0.42 mg, 0.89 mmol, 62%
over two steps). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO): δ [ppm] = 7.77 (d, 3J = 5.8 Hz,
1H), 7.07 (d, 3J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.86-6.84 (m, 3H), 6.49 (t, 3J = 5.5 Hz,
1H), 6.11 (dd, 3J = 5.8 Hz, 4J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 5.94 (d, 4J = 2.2 Hz, 1H),
3.99 (t, 3J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 3.92-3.85 (m, 1H), 3.69 (s, 3H), 3.54 (s, 3H),
3.36−3.32 (m, 2H), 2.65-2.56 (m, 2H), 2.37 (d, 3J = 6.9 Hz, 2H),
1.96-1.90 (m, 2H), 1.32 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO): δ [ppm] =
171.4, 166.0, 160.7, 157.1, 154.9, 148.7, 130.4, 130.2, 114.2, 100.9,
90.7, 77.7, 65.3, 54.6, 51.4, 49.5, 37.8, 28.9, 28.3. HPLC (10-90%): tR =
19.15 min. MS (ESI): m/z (%) = 474.2 [M + H]+, 418.3 [M - tBu + H]+,
374.3 [M - Boc + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pharmacophoric modifications lead to superpotent αvβ3 integrin ligands
with suppressed α5β1 activity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
