$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Butyl-L-ido-1-deoxynojirimycin (15).
Butyraldehyde (66 μL, 0.73 mmol) and NaCNBH3 (27 mg, 0.44 mmol) were
successively added to a solution of 13 (76 mg, 0.145 mmol) in CH3CN/AcOH
(1.45 mL, 30/1, v/v). The reaction mixture was stirred for 20 hours after
which sat. aq. NaHCO3 (5 mL) was added and the resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O (3×5 mL). The combined organic phases were dried
(Na2SO4) and concentrated to provide the crude N-butylated intermediate
(Rf = 0.5 in 4:1; PE:EtOAc). The crude intermediate was coevaporated with
dichloroethane and dissolved in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL). The solution was cooled
to 0°C and BCl3 (1.74 mL, 1M in CH2Cl2) was added. After stirring for 20
hours at 0°C MeOH (2 mL) was carefully added. The mixture was
concentrated and coevaporated with toluene. The residue was purified by
flash silica gel chromatography (0→ MeOH in CHCl3 + 1% NH4OH) to produce
15 (26 mg, 0.12 mmol) in 82% yield over two steps as a colorless oil.
N-[5-(Adamantan-1-yl-methoxy)-pentyl]-D-galacto-1-deoxynojirimycin (22).
Compound 22 (45 mg, 0.11 mmol) was synthesized from 19 (94 mg, 0.18 mmol)
and 1621 (90 mg, 0.36 mmol) in 61% yield as a colorless oil following the
reductive amination procedure as described for 15 and deprotected as
described for compound 4. Flash silica gel chromatography (0→ MeOH in
CHCl3 + 1% NH4OH). Rf N-alkylated intermediate = 0.68 (2:1; PE:EtOAc); Rf
22 = 0.19 (3:1; EtOAc:MeOH + 1% NH4OH). 1H NMR (400 MHz, MeOD, COSY) δ
3.97 (d, J = 12.0, 1H, H-6a), 3.88 (d, J = 12.0, 1H, H-6b), 3.63 - 3.54
(m, 1H, H-2), 3.50 - 3.46 (m, 1H, H-4), 3.41 (t, J = 6.1, 2H, CH2-5'
pentyl), 3.27 - 3.21 (m, 2H, H-1a, H-3), 3.12 - 3.04 (m, 1H, NCHH-1'
pentyl), 2.98 (s, 2H, OCH2), 2.95 - 2.86 (m, 1H, NCHH-1' pentyl), 2.65 -
2.54 (m, 2H, H-1b, H-5), 1.95 (s, 3H, 3×CH adamantane), 1.80 - 1.59 (m,
10H, CH2-2' CH2-4' pentyl, 3×CH2 adamantane), 1.56 (s, 6H, 3×CH2
adamantane), 1.47 - 1.39 (m, 2H, CH2-3' pentyl). 13C NMR (100 MHz, MeOD)
δ 83.3 (OCH2), 79.5 (C-3), 72.5 (OCH2-5' pentyl), 70.6 (C-4), 69.4 (C-2),
67.5 (C-5), 57.7 (C-6), 56.4 (C-1), 54.1 (NCH2- 1' pentyl), 41.0 (3×CH2
adamantane), 38.5 (3×CH2 adamantane), 35.3 (Cq adamantane), 30.5 (CH2-4'
pentyl), 29.9 (3×CH adamantane), 25.1 (CH2-2' pentyl), 24.7 (CH2-3'
pentyl). IR νmax(thin film)/ cm-1: 3349, 2900, 2848, 1735, 1652, 1452,
1093, 1030. [α]20D: +10.7 (c 0.28, CH3OH). HRMS: found 398.2892 [M+H]+,
calculatedfor [C22H39O5N1+H]+ 398.2901.
