$DATUM General Method C (Used for Compounds 17−21). Aldehyde (0.3 mmol) was
weighed into a 2 mL microwave vial. In a 20 mL scintillation vial, amine
(0.3 mmol) was weighed, and to this 2 mL of a 3:3:1 CH2Cl2/EtOH/AcOH
solution was added. The resulting solution was added to the mixture along
with polymer supported sodium cyanoborohydride, 2 mM/g (4.77 mmol). The
mixture was heated to 120 °C in the microwave for 10 min. The mixture was
filtered through a disposable filter funnel to remove the sodium
cyanoborohydride and evaporated overnight under reduced pressure. The
resulting solid was dissolved in DMSO and purified by reverse phase
preparative HPLC (20−100% MeCN in water with 0.5% TFA).
1-(4-Bromo-5-methylthiophen-2-yl)-N-(4-chlorobenzyl)-N-(pyridin-3-ylmethyl)methanamine
(17). By use of general method C, the title compound was afforded using
4-bromo-5-methylthiophene-2-carbaldehyde and [(4-chlorophenyl)methyl]
(3-pyridinylmethyl)amine as a white solid (72 mg, 170 μmol, 54%). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.68−8.64 (m, 1H), 8.61−8.57 (m, 1H), 8.16−8.11 (m,
1H), 7.68−7.62 (m, 1H), 7.40−7.34 (m, 4H), 6.92−6.89 (m, 1H), 3.71−3.63
(m, 4H), 3.57 (brs, 2H), 2.29 (s, 3H). LCMS: t R = 0.98 min, 100%. MS m/z
= 421 (M + H)+. HRMS calcd for C19H19BrClN2S (M + H)+ requires 421.0141,
found 421.0139.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, solid-supported reagent, polymer supported sodium
cyanoborohydride used
